    <h1>Facebook App Privacy Policy: What Meta App Review Requires and How to Pass It</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Published October 8, 2026</p>

    <p>Meta requires every Facebook app to provide a privacy policy URL before it can go live to the public. The privacy policy field sits in <strong>App Dashboard &gt; Settings &gt; Basic</strong> and must contain a publicly accessible HTTPS link that returns an HTTP 200 response. Without a valid URL in that field, you cannot submit your app for App Review, and no one outside your app's development team can use it.</p>

    <p>This guide covers exactly where Meta asks for the URL, what Facebook's Platform Terms require your policy to disclose, the data each Graph API permission returns and how to map it to privacy disclosures, Facebook Pages and Lead Ads requirements, and common reasons App Review rejects a privacy policy. If you need a finished policy without writing one from scratch, <a href="https://buildprivacypolicy.com/">generate a free privacy policy</a> and get a hosted URL you can paste directly into your App Dashboard.</p>

